From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: CSIDL_COMMON_FAVORITES is the caller's own Favorites (9102)

On Windows Vista and later CSIDL_COMMON_FAVORITES and CSIDL_FAVORITES are
both FOLDERID_Favorites, a per-user folder. Wine read the common one from
HKLM's Common Favorites, which the account that built the prefix filled
with its own profile's folder: in the shared prefix every person got
C:\users\sgsystem\Favorites -- the SYSTEM account's, which is now closed to
them (sg-session makes SYSTEM's profile private, as Windows'
systemprofile is). SHGetFolderPath maps it to the caller's Favorites.

Gate test/commonfav-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit). Mutant:
SG_MUTANT_COMMON_FAVORITES_HKLM.
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
@@ -2948,6 +2948,14 @@
                 break;
             }
     }
+    /* Stained Glass OS 9102: CSIDL_COMMON_FAVORITES is the caller's own
+     * Favorites, as on Windows Vista and later (both are FOLDERID_Favorites,
+     * a per-user folder). Wine read it from HKLM's Common Favorites, which
+     * the prefix's first account filled with its own profile's folder: in
+     * the shared prefix every person got the SYSTEM account's Favorites. */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_COMMON_FAVORITES_HKLM
+    if (folder == CSIDL_COMMON_FAVORITES) folder = CSIDL_FAVORITES;
+#endif
     szTemp[0] = 0;
     type = CSIDL_Data[folder].type;
     switch (type)
